Feature: Loud and quiet drones
  In the [[v4 rules]], a drone is [[loud]] or [[quiet]]. A loud drone sends its telemetry and the
  picture of its camera to its team. A quiet drone sends nothing: it still hears the orders of its
  commander, but its team has only where it last heard from it, and its camera adds nothing to the
  map of the team.

  The radio of a loud drone can be found. A fort or the spire that a team holds takes a
  [[bearing]] on each loud enemy drone within 400 m: the direction to it, not the place. Two
  bearings on one drone cross where it is, and the team sees it there. A quiet drone gives no
  bearing.

  Expectation: A quiet drone hears its team but sends nothing
    Given the emission of the first Blue drone is quiet
    And the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    When the first Blue drone flies to the west circle
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is in contact
    And the first Blue drone on the Blue map is last in contact

  Expectation: Two bearings find a loud drone that nobody sees
    Given the direction finding is on
    And the centre tower is held by Blue
    And the towers held by Blue are 2
    And the Red scout is high between the Blue home tower and the centre tower
    And the emission of the Red scout is loud
    Then the bearings on the Red scout are 2
    And the Red scout on the Blue map is seen

  Expectation: One bearing gives the direction, not the place
    Given the direction finding is on
    And the centre tower is neutral
    And the Red scout is high between the Blue home tower and the centre tower
    And the emission of the Red scout is loud
    Then the bearings on the Red scout are 1
    And the Red scout on the Blue map is unknown

  Expectation: A quiet drone gives no bearing
    Given the direction finding is on
    And the centre tower is held by Blue
    And the towers held by Blue are 2
    And the Red scout is high between the Blue home tower and the centre tower
    And the emission of the Red scout is quiet
    Then the bearings on the Red scout are 0
    And the Red scout on the Blue map is unknown

  Expectation: A quiet drone does not report its battery
    Given the emission of the first Blue drone is quiet
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 100 s
    And the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    When the first Blue drone flies quiet for 10 seconds
    Then the battery of the first Blue drone is 90 s
    And the battery of the first Blue drone on the Blue map is 100 s

  Expectation: A quiet drone goes loud at its bingo battery
    The failsafe of the drone sends its telemetry again when its battery gets down to 60 s, so
    that its commander can bring it home.

    Given the emission of the first Blue drone is quiet
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 65 s
    And the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    When the first Blue drone flies quiet for 10 seconds
    Then the emission of the first Blue drone is loud
